{"name":"Sweet Angel","hex":"#f5c8bb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"angel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An incorporeal and holy or semidivine messenger from a deity or other divine entity, traditionally depicted as a youthful, winged figure in flowing robes.\n\n One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues.","One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To support by donating money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet Angel (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sweet Angel is a 2011 Sri Lankan Sinhala drama thriller film directed by Nishantha Weerasingha and produced by Susan Fernando for Lionel Films. It stars Suresh Gamage and new coming actress Deepa Chandi in lead roles along with Manel Wanaguru and Sanju Rodrigo. Music co-composed by Madhava Hawawasam and Lassana Jayasekara. It is the 1159th Sri Lankan film in the Sinhala cinema."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Angel_(film)"},{"title":"Edna Rose Ritchings","blocks":[{"text":"Edna Rose Ritchings was the symbolic maintainer of the International Peace Mission movement. She is also known as Sweet Angel in the movement, or as Mrs. S. A. Divine or Mother Divine because she was the widow of the movement's leader, Father Divine. She assisted Father Divine, who claimed to be God, in his declining years. They lived in a manor home, which doubled as a Peace Mission headquarters and church known as the Woodmont manor & estate from 1953. It is located at Gladwyne, Pennsylvania, a Philadelphia suburb. Father Divine died in 1965 and was later interred in a crypt and mausoleum on the premises. The Woodmont estate continued to be the home of Mrs. Divine."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edna_Rose_Ritchings"},{"title":"Sweetness","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetness is a basic taste most commonly perceived when eating foods rich in sugar. Sweet tastes are generally regarded as pleasurable. In addition to sugars like sucrose, many other chemical compounds are sweet, including aldehydes, ketones, and sugar alcohols. Some are sweet at very low concentrations, allowing their use as non-caloric sugar substitutes. Such non-sugar sweeteners include saccharin, aspartame, sucralose and stevia. Other compounds, such as miraculin, may alter perception of sweetness itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strawberry_shortcake.jpg/330px-Strawberry_shortcake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetness"},{"title":"Angel","blocks":[{"text":"An angel is a spiritual, heavenly, or supernatural entity, often depicted as humanoid with bird-like wings, frequently in the role as a messenger or intermediary between God and humanity in various traditions like the Abrahamic religions. Other roles include protectors and guides for humans, such as guardian angels, and servants of God. In Western belief-systems the term is often used to distinguish benevolent from malevolent intermediary beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg/330px-Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Boys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg/500px-Boys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Boys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg/1280px-Boys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Boys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg/500px-Boys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boys Pilfering Molasses – On The Quays, New Orleans, 1853 painting by George Henry Hall","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Gray1018.png/250px-Gray1018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/Gray1018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Gray1018.png/250px-Gray1018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sweetness is perceived by the taste buds.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray1018.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Gut_Brain_Reward_Pathway.webp/250px-Gut_Brain_Reward_Pathway.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/Gut_Brain_Reward_Pathway.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Gut_Brain_Reward_Pathway.webp/250px-Gut_Brain_Reward_Pathway.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gut-brain reward pathway","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGut_Brain_Reward_Pathway.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Overview_of_reward_structures_in_the_human_brain.jpg/5